SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$LOA Table 5.3.4.1 Prescribed accepted development - Dwelling house character overlay, small lot, raising only (rows 4587/4589 already in brisbane.json) / High density residential zone$q$, 'LEVEL_OF_ASSESSMENT', $q$|  | Building work if in the Dwelling house character overlay and on a small lot where:
- outside the building envelope contained in the acceptable outcomes in section A or section B of the Dwelling house (small lot) code; or
- outside the building envelope contained in a development approval to the extent it differs from (a) above. | If for a dwelling house involving only raising a building where:
- the side boundary setbacks comply with the setbacks under the Building Regulation 2021;
- the maximum height does not exceed 9.5m above ground level; or
- the maximum height does not exceed 11.5m above ground level where within the 3 or 4 storey mix zone precinct of the Low-medium density residential zone;
- any windows that are within 2m at ground level or 9m above ground level of a neighbouring dwelling house (refer to Figure g in the Dwelling house (small lot) code):
- are offset from the window of a habitable room in the adjacent dwelling house to limit direct outlook as shown in Figure h in the Dwelling house (small lot) code; or
- have sill heights of 1.5m above floor level; or
- are covered by fixed obscure glazing in any part of the window below 1.5m above floor level; or
- have fixed external screens; or
- in the case of screening for a ground floor level, fencing to a height of 1.5m above ground floor level;
- any screening devices required above, are:
- solid translucent screens, perforated or slatted panels or fixed louvres that have a maximum of 25% openings, with a maximum opening dimension of 50mm, that are permanently fixed and durable (refer to Figure j and Figure i in the Dwelling house (small lot) code);
- offset a minimum of 0.3m from the face of any window;
- may be hinged to facilitate emergency egress only.
Note—For the purpose of this provision the setbacks of the Building Regulation 2021 are to be read as taken to the wall, not the outermost projection.
