SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$LOA Planning Regulation 2017 sch 6 pt 2 s2(2) State accepted MCU for a dwelling house (Planning Regulation 2017 sch 6 pt 2 s2(2)) / High density residential zone$q$, 'LEVEL_OF_ASSESSMENT', $q$(2) A material change of use of premises for a dwelling house, if— (a) the material change of use is for a residential purpose in a residential zone other than a medium density residential zone or high density residential zone; and (b) the material change of use does not involve a basement or an underground parking area; and (c) 1 of the following applies— (i) no relevant overlay applies to the premises; (ii) only an overlay about bush fire hazards applies to the premises and the premises are less than 2,000m2; (iii) a relevant overlay applies to the premises and the application of the overlay does not result in the material change of use being categorised as assessable development.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $q$https://www.legislation.qld.gov.au/view/whole/xml/inforce/current/sl-2017-0078$q$, $q$Level: Not available in HDR. Conditions: State-level accepted MCU for a dwelling house excludes the medium density residential zone and the high density residential zone.$q$, NULL);
SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$overlay Traditional building character overlay Table 8.2.22.3 PO1/AO1.2$q$, 'OTHER', $q$AO1.2
Development for a building which is not on a rear lot is set back from any road alignment, excluding eaves, awnings, stairs and garage, within 20% of the average front setback of the nearest residential buildings constructed in 1946 or earlier fronting the same street.
Note—Additional buildings by way of infill development may be set further back on this site, subject to meeting other code requirements. Where the site contains a building constructed in 1946 or earlier, it should be retained at the front of the site and any new infill placed behind/beside. Sliding a building constructed in 1946 or earlier back with infill at the front of the site is not consistent with desired traditional setting outcomes.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', NULL, NULL, $q$Traditional building character (design) overlay code (8.2.22)$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/150/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$Front setback within 20% of average of nearest pre-1947 buildings (AO1.2, alternative provision item 10); garage setback similar to nearby pre-1947 garages (AO2.1, item 10); Sherwood-Graceville: rear 6m, 2 storeys, carport width 3.5m forward of facade (planning only); makes dwelling house building work code assessable (Table 5.10.21).$q$, NULL);
SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$overlay Dwelling house character overlay Table 5.10.9$q$, 'OTHER', $q$Note—The Dwelling house character overlay applies to land identified within the Low density residential zone, Low-medium density residential zone, Medium density residential zone, High density residential zone, Character residential zone or Tourist accommodation zone. The category of assessment for a dwelling house outside of the Dwelling house character overlay is specified in section 5.5 and section 5.7.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', NULL, NULL, $q$No applicable overlay code (Table 5.10.9 refers to Dwelling house code / Dwelling house (small lot) code)$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/483/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$Changes category of development for new dwelling houses and extensions in LDR/LMR/MDR/HDR/CR/Tourist accommodation zones to accepted-subject-to-requirements/code assessment against the dwelling house codes; Table 5.3.4.1 sets prescribed accepted minor structures (shed 10m2/3m, patio 16m2/3m, carport dimensions) for small lots. Does not itself vary setback numbers.$q$, NULL);
SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$overlay Flood overlay Dwelling house code note; s1.7.2$q$, 'OTHER', $q$Note—Where the land is identified in an overlay such as the Bushfire overlay map, Flood overlay map, Landslide overlay map, Significant landscape trees overlay map or Waterway corridors overlay map, additional provisions relating to that overlay also apply. For example, minimum floor levels for a dwelling house on a site subject to certain types of flooding, are identified in the Flood overlay code.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', NULL, NULL, $q$Flood overlay code (8.2.11)$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/162/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$Sets minimum floor levels / designated flood hazard area for QDC MP3.5 (s1.7.2); not a setback/height variation per se but may require raised houses (Dwelling house code PO2(d) allows extra height to the extent required for flood immunity). Not extracted in detail.$q$, NULL);

SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$9.3.7.3 Table 9.3.7.3.A, PO2/AO2$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO2
Development in the Low density residential zone, Character residential zone, 2 storey mix zone precinct of the Low–medium density residential zone, Rural residential zone, Environmental management zone, Rural zone or Emerging community zone results in a maximum building height of 9.5m and:
- 2 storeys; or
- 1 storey if the development also includes a space that is situated between one floor level and the floor level next above, or if there is no floor above, the ceiling or roof above that contains only a bathroom, shower room, laundry, water closet, or other sanitary compartment.
Editor's note—This acceptable outcome is only for the maximum building height. Side boundary setbacks are provided in accordance with the Queensland Development Code; which vary according to the height of the building.
Editor's note—For the purposes of determining compliance with AO2 reference is to be made to section 1.7.7.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 15277$q$, NULL, $q$Dwelling house code$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/162/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$Building height per SC1.2: vertical distance between ground level and the highest point on the roof (excl. aerial, chimney, flagpole, load-bearing antenna), or number of storeys above ground level. s1.7.7 reduces storey count by 1 where a sanitary-only intermediate space exists.$q$, $q$dh_max_height_low_density$q$);
