SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$9.3.8.3 Table 9.3.8.3.A, PO2/AO2$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO2
Development is contained within:
- the building envelope for the site, created by applying:
- the acceptable outcome for maximum building height;
- the acceptable outcome for front, rear and side boundary setbacks;
- acceptable outcomes for built to boundary walls in so far as these determine the building envelope; or
- the approved building envelope for the site to the extent of any inconsistency with (a).
Note—Refer to Figure a for examples of the building envelope for a dwelling house on a small lot.
Note—The building envelope is not the developable area or building extent, but a three-dimensional envelope that limits the extent of a building in any direction.
Note—This acceptable outcome can be demonstrated by preparing a building envelope plan, elevations and sections.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 15302$q$, NULL, $q$Dwelling house (small lot) code$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/163/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, NULL, $q$sl_building_envelope$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "BCC.sl_building_envelope", "instrument_version": "BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18", "topic": "OTHER", "title": "9.3.8.3 Table 9.3.8.3.A, PO2/AO2", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_OTHER", "operator": "=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "AO2\nDevelopment is contained within:\n- the building envelope for the site, created by applying:\n- the acceptable outcome for maximum building height;\n- the acceptable outcome for front, rear and side boundary setbacks;\n- acceptable outcomes for built to boundary walls in so far as these determine the building envelope; or\n- the approved building envelope for the site to the extent of any inconsistency with (a).\nNote—Refer to Figure a for examples of the building envelope for a dwelling house on a small lot.\nNote—The building envelope is not the developable area or building extent, but a three-dimensional envelope that limits the extent of a building in any direction.\nNote—This acceptable outcome can be demonstrated by preparing a building envelope plan, elevations and sections.", "extracted_value": true, "extracted_operator": "="}, "unit": null, "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2026-09-18", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "BRISBANE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:LOW_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:LOW_MEDIUM_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:MEDIUM_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:CHARACTER_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:RURAL_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:EMERGING_COMMUNITY"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:ENVIRONMENTAL_MANAGEMENT"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:RURAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:TOWNSHIP"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:HIGH_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A", "CLASS_1"], "sources": [{"key": "sl_building_envelope", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"within_building_envelope\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": true, \"unit\": null, \"conditions\": [\"envelope = max height AO + front/rear/side setback AOs + built-to-boundary AOs\", \"or approved building envelope prevails to extent of inconsistency\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null}\nLot conditions (not encoded): Section A - small lot (lot < 450 m2, or rear lot < 600 m2 excl. access way) that is 180 m2 or greater\nStructure scope 'development incl. dwelling house, secondary dwelling, domestic outbuildings' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES\nResearcher notes: Brisbane City Plan 2014 s1.6 Table 1.6.1 item 6 (s32(b) BA, s6 BR): 'Qualitative statements and quantifiable standards for matters provided for under performance criteria 4 under QDC parts MP 1.1 and MP 1.2 ...' | Table 1.6.1 item 10 (ss32(c) and 33 BA): 'Alternative provisions to performance criteria 1 under QDC parts MP1.1 and MP1.2 of the QDC boundary clearance and site cover provisions for particular buildings' | Table 1.6.1 item 11 (ss32(c) and 33 BA): 'Alternative provisions to performance criteria 2 under QDC parts MP1.1 and 1.2 of the QDC boundary clearance and site cover provisions for particular buildings'. NOTE: Table 1.6.1 still refers to QDC MP1.1/MP1.2; no reference to the Queensland Housing Code was found anywhere in City Plan v37.00/2026. Listed as 'PO2 and AO2' in items 6, 10 and 11."}$q$::jsonb);
