SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "BCC.sl_garage_street_setback", "instrument_version": "BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18", "topic": "GARAGE.FRONTAGE", "title": "9.3.8.3 Table 9.3.8.3.A, PO5/AO5(c)", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_GARAGE_CARPORT", "operator": ">=", "value": 5.5, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2026-09-18", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "BRISBANE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:LOW_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:LOW_MEDIUM_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:MEDIUM_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:CHARACTER_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:RURAL_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:EMERGING_COMMUNITY"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:ENVIRONMENTAL_MANAGEMENT"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:RURAL"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:TOWNSHIP"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:HIGH_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A"], "sources": [{"key": "sl_garage_street_setback", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"min_garage_street_frontage_setback\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": 5.5, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"applies 'in addition to either (a) where the setback is less than 5.5m or (b)(i)'\"], \"exceptions\": [\"AO13.4 steep site (slope 1 in 4 or greater) car accommodation may be closer to the road alignment than the house\"], \"formula_text\": null}\nLot conditions (not encoded): Section A - small lot (lot < 450 m2, or rear lot < 600 m2 excl. access way) that is 180 m2 or greater\nStructure scope 'garage' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES\nResearcher notes: Table 1.6.1 item 10 (ss32(c) and 33 BA): 'Alternative provisions to performance criteria 1 under QDC parts MP1.1 and MP1.2 of the QDC boundary clearance and site cover provisions for particular buildings'. NOTE: Table 1.6.1 still refers to QDC MP1.1/MP1.2; no reference to the Queensland Housing Code was found anywhere in City Plan v37.00/2026. Text says 'garages' only - carports are not expressly captured by AO5(c) (compare AO22.2 'covered car parking' for < 180 m2 lots). AO12.1(c) also requires 1 parking space forward of a garage (not on secondary frontage)."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$BCC.sl_garage_street_setback@2026-09-18$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$9.3.8.3 Table 9.3.8.3.A, PO6/AO6(a)-(b)$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO6
Development results in a minimum side boundary setback that is:
- 1m for habitable spaces; or
- 0.5m and a maximum height of 3.5m for non-habitable spaces only for a maximum length of:
- 15m, where located in the Low–medium density residential zone, Medium density residential zone or High density residential zone; or
- 9m, where in the Low density residential zone or the Character residential zone; or
- 0m where:
- matching the extent of an existing built to boundary wall on the adjoining property; or
- the adjoining property is 300m2 or less and in the Residential zone category other than in the Character zone precinct of the Character residential zone; or
- on a lot with an average width of 7.5m or less where the adjoining property is 300m2 or less and in the Residential zone category other than in the Character zone precinct of the Character residential zone and the adjoining property has no existing built to the boundary wall; or
- on a lot with an average width of more than 7.5m in the Low density residential zone or the Infill housing zone precinct of the Character residential zone where the registered owner of the adjoining premises does not object to a setback less than AO6(b) but only for non-habitable spaces, a maximum height of 3m and a maximum length of 9m; or
- located within an approved building envelope for the site to the extent of any inconsistency with (a), (b) or (c).
Note—AO6(c)(ii) and (iii) apply to the development of a dwelling house at the same time as an adjoining dwelling house or adjoining dwelling houses developed at separate times.
Editor's note—For the purposes of determining compliance with AO6 reference is to be made to section 1.7.6.
Editor's note—For the purpose of satisfying AO6(c)(iv), confirmation in writing in the form of a statutory declaration from the registered owner of the adjoining premises is required to be submitted to demonstrate compliance.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 15306$q$, NULL, $q$Dwelling house (small lot) code$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/163/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$Setback measured per SC1.2 'setback' definition: shortest horizontal distance from the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the lot boundary. s1.7.6 deems compliance where only an eave or sunhood/the like exceeds the setback benchmark.$q$, $q$sl_side_setback$q$);
