SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$9.3.8.3 Table 9.3.8.3.A, PO7/AO7$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO7
Development results in a minimum rear boundary setback that is:
- 6m, where on a lot with an average depth of more than 25m; or
- on a lot with an average depth of 25m or less:
- 3m, for a part of a building or structure up to 4.5m high;
- 4.5m, for a part of a building or structure over 4.5m high.
- located within an approved building envelope for the site to the extent of any inconsistency with (a) or (b).
Editor's note—For the purposes of determining compliance with AO7 reference is to be made to section 1.7.6.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 15307$q$, NULL, $q$Dwelling house (small lot) code$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/163/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$Setback measured per SC1.2 'setback' definition: shortest horizontal distance from the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the lot boundary. s1.7.6 deems compliance where only an eave or sunhood/the like exceeds the setback benchmark. 'Average depth' is not defined in the SC1.2 extract reviewed (average width is).$q$, $q$sl_rear_setback$q$);
