INSERT INTO rule_relationships (from_rule_version_id, to_rule_id, type, basis_provision_id, verification, notes) VALUES ($q$BCC.slb_site_cover@2026-09-18$q$, $q$QDC11.A3.SITE_COVER$q$, 'OVERRIDES', p('QLD_BUILDING_ACT_1975@2026-02-01', 's 33'), 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', 'Alternative provision (Building Act s33(4)): QDC applies only to the extent this provision does not. Scope must be confirmed per rule (zone/precinct/structure).');
SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$9.3.8.3 Table 9.3.8.3.A Section B, PO20/AO20$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$AO20
Development results in a maximum impervious area:
- of 70% of the total site area; or 
- that is in accordance with an approved development footprint plan for the site.
Note—In interpreting AO20, impervious areas are areas formed or covered by materials that prevent the infiltration of water into the ground below and prevent planting in-ground, including:
- roofed areas, manoeuvring areas, hardstand or swimming pools;
- other areas covered by tiles, bricks, compacted gravel, artificial turf or concrete.
Note—Where demonstrating compliance with PO28/AO28.1 in the Subdivision code, compliance with this acceptable outcome must be shown on a development footprint plan.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 60875$q$, NULL, $q$Dwelling house (small lot) code$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/163/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, NULL, $q$slb_impervious_area$q$);
