SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$5.3.4 Table 5.3.4.1 (Building work, Dwelling house character overlay, small lot)$q$, 'ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT', $q$|  | Building work if in the Dwelling house character overlay and on a small lot:
- outside the building envelope contained in the acceptable outcomes in section A or section B of the Dwelling house (small lot) code; or
- outside the building envelope contained in a development approval to the extent it differs from (a) above. | If for a dwelling house involving one or more of the following:
- aerials or sewer vents on the roof;
- enclosing under an existing house (except where located in an overlay that makes such development assessable e.g. Flood overlay and Heritage overlay);
- 1 unenclosed patio or gazebo (maximum roofed area 16m2 and maximum height 3m);
- a swimming pool and/or spa (of any size) and unenclosed ancillary shade structures. Any shade structures are to have a maximum roofed area 10m2 and maximum height 3m;
- unenclosed roofed ground-level walkway (maximum 1.3m wide and maximum height of 2.5m above finished ground level to the underside of the ceiling) between the building components;
- 1 shed (maximum roofed area 10m2 and maximum height 3m);
- roof structures over existing decks, balconies (maximum height 9.5m above ground level);
- gatehouse (maximum roofed area 3m2 and maximum height 3m);
- 1 single carport where:
- maximum depth 6m, excluding eaves;
- maximum width 3m, excluding eaves;
- 1 double carport on a lot 180m2 or greater only, where:
- maximum depth 6m, excluding eaves;
- maximum width 6m, excluding eaves;
- minimum side boundary setback 1.5m;
- minimum front boundary setback 2m;
- maximum crossover width 4.5m;
- on a lot with a street frontage width of 15m or greater, and the total building footprint of the dwelling and carport does not exceed 50%.
Note—Unless specified, the above building works are still subject to the siting provisions of the Building Regulation 2021.
Note—For the purpose of this provision, the setbacks of the Building Regulation 2021 are to be read as taken to the wall, not the outermost projection. |$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 4589$q$, NULL, $q$Part 5 Table 5.3.4.1 Prescribed accepted development$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/222/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, NULL, $q$pad_dhc_small_lot_minor_structures$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "BCC.pad_dhc_small_lot_minor_structures", "instrument_version": "BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18", "topic": "OUTBUILDING.SIZE", "title": "5.3.4 Table 5.3.4.1 (Building work, Dwelling house character overlay, small lot)", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT", "measurement": "SCHEME_OUTBUILDING_SIZE", "operator": "<=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "|  | Building work if in the Dwelling house character overlay and on a small lot:\n- outside the building envelope contained in the acceptable outcomes in section A or section B of the Dwelling house (small lot) code; or\n- outside the building envelope contained in a development approval to the extent it differs from (a) above. | If for a dwelling house involving one or more of the following:\n- aerials or sewer vents on the roof;\n- enclosing under an existing house (except where located in an overlay that makes such development assessable e.g. Flood overlay and Heritage overlay);\n- 1 unenclosed patio or gazebo (maximum roofed area 16m2 and maximum height 3m);\n- a swimming pool and/or spa (of any size) and unenclosed ancillary shade structures. Any shade structures are to have a maximum roofed area 10m2 and maximum height 3m;\n- unenclosed roofed ground-level walkway (maximum 1.3m wide and maximum height of 2.5m above finished ground level to the underside of the ceiling) between the building components;\n- 1 shed (maximum roofed area 10m2 and maximum height 3m);\n- roof structures over existing decks, balconies (maximum height 9.5m above ground level);\n- gatehouse (maximum roofed area 3m2 and maximum height 3m);\n- 1 single carport where:\n- maximum depth 6m, excluding eaves;\n- maximum width 3m, excluding eaves;\n- 1 double carport on a lot 180m2 or greater only, where:\n- maximum depth 6m, excluding eaves;\n- maximum width 6m, excluding eaves;\n- minimum side boundary setback 1.5m;\n- minimum front boundary setback 2m;\n- maximum crossover width 4.5m;\n- on a lot with a street frontage width of 15m or greater, and the total building footprint of the dwelling and carport does not exceed 50%.\nNote—Unless specified, the above building works are still subject to the siting provisions of the Building Regulation 2021.\nNote—For the purpose of this provision, the setbacks of the Building Regulation 2021 are to be read as taken to the wall, not the outermost projection. |", "extracted_value": null, "extracted_operator": "conditional"}, "unit": null, "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2026-09-18", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "BRISBANE"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "BCC:OV:DWELLING_HOUSE_CHARACTER_OVERLAY"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "BCC:HIGH_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "BCC:OV:DWELLING_HOUSE_CHARACTER_OVERLAY"}], "subjects": ["POOL", "CLASS_10A", "CLASS_1", "OUTDOOR_STRUCTURE"], "sources": [{"key": "pad_dhc_small_lot_minor_structures", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"prescribed_accepted_minor_structures\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": null, \"conditions\": [\"1 unenclosed patio or gazebo max roofed area 16m2, max height 3m\", \"swimming pool/spa any size; shade structures max 10m2, max height 3m\", \"1 shed max roofed area 10m2, max height 3m\", \"gatehouse max 3m2 / 3m\", \"roofed walkway max 1.3m wide, 2.5m to underside of ceiling\", \"roof over existing decks/balconies max 9.5m above ground\", \"1 single carport max depth 6m, max width 3m excl. eaves\", \"1 double carport (lot 180m2+): max 6m x 6m, min side setback 1.5m, min front setback 2m, max crossover 4.5m, frontage 15m or greater, dwelling+carport footprint <= 50%\"], \"exceptions\": [\"still subject to Building Regulation 2021 siting provisions, measured to the wall not outermost projection\"], \"formula_text\": null}\nLot conditions (not encoded): small lot; building work outside the small-lot code building envelope\nStructure scope 'patio/gazebo, swimming pool/spa + shade structures, shed, carports, gatehouse, roofed walkway, roof over existing decks' mapped by keyword to ['POOL', 'CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1', 'OUTDOOR_STRUCTURE']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO\nResearcher notes: Planning-scheme category (not assessable under the scheme) - not an alternative provision. The Notes expressly keep the 'siting provisions of the Building Regulation 2021' (i.e. QDC/QHC) applicable. Wording 'Building work if in the Dwelling house character overlay and on a small lot: outside the building envelope...' is as published."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$BCC.pad_dhc_small_lot_minor_structures@2026-09-18$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$BCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2026-09-18$q$, $q$5.3.4 Table 5.3.4.1 (Building work, Dwelling house character overlay, small lot, within envelope)$q$, 'ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT', $q$|  | Building work if in the Dwelling house character overlay and on a small lot where:
- within the building envelope contained in the acceptable outcomes in section A or section B of the Dwelling house (small lot) code; or
- within the building envelope contained in a development approval to the extent it differs from (a) above. | If for a dwelling house involving only renovations and extensions to an existing building where:
- the total building footprint of the dwelling house including extensions does not exceed 55% of the site area on a lot less than 180m2, or 50% of the site area on any other lot;
- any roof deck or viewing platform that forms part of the renovation or extension is set back at least 1.5m from the side boundary and is no more than 7m above ground level or the height of an upper storey roof, whichever is the lesser;
- any balconies, terraces, decks or roof decks that form part of the renovation or extension that result in a direct view into windows of habitable rooms, balconies, terraces and decks in an adjacent dwelling house, ensure that view is screened from floor level to a height of 1.5m above floor level;
- any renovation or extension within 2m at ground level or 9m above ground level of a neighbouring dwelling house (refer to Figure g in the Dwelling house (small lot) code) only incorporates windows where they:
- are offset from the window of a habitable room in the adjacent dwelling house to limit direct outlook as shown in Figure h in the Dwelling house (small lot) code; or
- have sill heights of 1.5m above floor level; or
- are covered by fixed obscure glazing in any part of the window below 1.5m above floor level; or
- have fixed external screens; or
- in the case of screening for a ground floor level, fencing to a height of 1.5m above ground floor level;
- any screening devices required by (c) or (d) above, are:
- solid translucent screens, perforated or slatted panels or fixed louvres that have a maximum of 25% openings, with a maximum opening dimension of 50mm, that are permanently fixed and durable (refer to Figure i and Figure j in the Dwelling house (small lot) code);
- offset a minimum of 0.3m from the face of any window;
- may be hinged to facilitate emergency egress only. |$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 4587$q$, NULL, $q$Part 5 Table 5.3.4.1 Prescribed accepted development$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.brisbane.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/222/0/false/28-Sep-2026/false$q$, NULL, $q$pad_dhc_small_lot_renovation_footprint$q$);
